{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":31591,"duration_api_ms":31567,"num_turns":2,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c4939c21-088e-45b3-913b-2bb6ec49f2a8","total_cost_usd":0.256622,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33862,"cache_read_input_tokens":32689,"output_tokens":1145,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33862,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":3,"outputTokens":1145,"cacheReadInputTokens":32689,"cacheCreationInputTokens":33862,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.256622,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"rulings":[{"amendment_id":"fr-1-7e77d2a4","decision":"accept","rationale":"The omission is factually confirmed by all three parties: the extreme-scale test (1L vs 1000L) checks per-liter concentration deltas but entirely omits the Monod factor comparison block present in the primary test (10L vs 100L). Reviewer 2's objection that per_guild_monod_uses_concentration_not_total already covers Monod factors at multiple volumes has merit as a redundancy argument, but it does not outweigh the value of adding the check here. First, the amendment itself acknowledges the per-liter delta is the stronger assertion — the Monod factor block is a complementary, low-cost addition that makes the extreme-scale test self-contained and internally consistent with the primary test. Second, the dedicated Monod test and the integration-style volume-independence test exercise different code paths and verify different properties (isolated Monod correctness vs. end-to-end volume independence); having Monod factor equivalence confirmed alongside delta equivalence at 1000x scale provides meaningful defense-in-depth. Third, the cost is negligible — either copy the block or factor it into a shared helper, which also improves maintainability. The 2-1 consensus in favor of acceptance reflects the correct balance: a small, low-risk improvement that closes a real asymmetry between the two tests."}],"summary":"One disputed amendment (fr-1-7e77d2a4) ruled ACCEPT. The extreme-scale volume-independence test genuinely omits the Monod factor verification block present in the primary test. While a separate dedicated Monod test exists, adding the same block to the extreme-scale integration test is a low-cost improvement that makes the test self-contained and provides defense-in-depth at the 1000x volume ratio where floating-point precision issues are most likely to surface."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"71288523-ad3b-4d56-9084-1606c29d7fe7"}
